<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Australia shutdown Geelong crude unit.</title>
<headline>Shell Australia shutdown Geelong crude unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shell Company of Australia SHELL has shutdown a 74,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit (CDU) at its Geelong refinery over the weekend for planned maintenance, a company source said on Monday.</p>
<p>Some smaller units, including a platformer, were also shutdown for maintenance.</p>
<p>The maintenance period at the 115,000-bpd Geelong refinery is expected to last until early August, said the source.</p>
<p>Shell also owns the 80,000-bpd Clyde refinery near Sydney, but has no maintenance plans for the refinery this year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3082)</p>
